==Latin==

===Etymology===
From {{af|la|tam||alt2=-em}}. Last particle in {{m|la|īdem}}. Compare with its later doublet: {{m|la|tandem}}, both with original meaning supposedly ''"so(much)ever"''.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA}}
* Note: unlike in {{m|la|tametsī}}, the graphic ''m'' does represent the bilabial nasal /m/.

===Conjunction===
{{head|la|conjunction}}

# {{lb|la|usually|postpositive|also|initial|and|final}} [[however]], [[in spite of]] this
## {{q|preceded by {{m|la|et}}, {{m|la|atque}}/{{m|la|ac}}, {{m|la|neque}}/{{m|la|nec}}, {{m|la|at}}, {{m|la|sed}}, {{m|la|vērum}}}}
##: {{uxi|la|ac '''tamen'''...|and '''yet'''...}}
# {{q|expressing a concession}} [[nevertheless]], [[yet]], [[still]]
#: {{Q|la|Terence|Andria|864|quote=''SIMO'' Nihil audiō! Ego iam tē commōtum reddam! ''DAVUS'' Tamen etsī hoc vērum·st? ''SIMO'' '''Tamen!'''|t=''SI'' I'm not listening! Your heart strings are about to get a real good tugging! ''DA'' Even if it's true? ''SI'' '''Even so!'''|lit=...I'm about to make you greatly moved...}}
# [[all the same]], [[just the same]] {{gl|in spite of appearances of the contrary}}
#: {{Q|la|Plautus|Pseudolus|405|quote={{...}}vīginti minās, quae nūsquam nunc sunt gentium, inveniam '''tamen.'''|t={{...}}those twenty minas, which are currently nowhere to be found, I'll find them '''all the same.'''}}
# {{q|in an aside}} [[although]], [[even if]]
# {{q|in a limiting clause}} {{lb|la|also|with|[[ut]]|or|[[ne]]}} [[at least]]

